\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Wise men, seeking Jesus, 
\par Travelled from afar,
\par Guided on their journey
\par By a beauteous star.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. But if we desire Him,
\par He is close at hand;
\par For our native country
\par Is our Holy Land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Prayerful souls may find Him
\par By our quiet lakes,
\par Meet Him on our hillsides
\par When the morning breaks.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In our fertile cornfields
\par While the sheaves are bound,
\par In our busy markets,
\par Jesus may be found.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Fishermen talk with Him
\par By the great North Sea,
\par As the first desciples
\par Did in Galilee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Every peaceful village
\par In our land might be
\par Made by Jesu's presence
\par Like sweet Bethany.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. He is more than near us,
\par If we love Him well;
\par For He seeketh ever
\par In our hearts to dwell.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

